Invoking $\sum_{i=1}^n{a_i} \leq S$, we obtain $a_i \leq \frac{S}{n-(i-1)}$, for all $i \in \{1,\ldots,n\}$. From the preceding relation and that $\prod_{j=1}^na_j \geq P$, we can obtain $a_1 \geq (n-1)!P/S^{n-1}.$
